==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|helpanan|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|kelb-||kelp-|lang=ang}}. Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|helpa#Old Frisian|helpa}} (West Frisian {{term|helpe|lang=fy}}), Old High German {{term|helfan|lang=goh}} (German {{term|helfen|lang=de}}), Old Saxon {{term|helpan#Old Saxon|helpan}} (Dutch {{term|helpen|lang=nl}}), Old Norse {{term|hjalpa}} (Icelandic {{term|hjálpa|lang=is}}, Swedish {{term|hjälpa}}), Gothic {{term|𐌷𐌹𐌻𐍀𐌰𐌽|tr=hilpan|sc=Goth}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhelpɑn/|lang=ang}}

